IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 162 -- loans and quasi-loans to directors, credit transactions and related arrangements.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part sgb2. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
--
-- HOW IT READS. A "restricted transaction" (s 162(1)) is one of six kinds of dealing by a company with a "relevant director". The company (other than an
-- exempt private company) must not make one (s 162(2)), subject to the exceptions of s 162(3) and (4) and ss 163A and 163B. A "relevant director" is a
-- director of the company or of a company that s 6 deems related to it, and s 162(8) adds the director's spouse and children of the listed kinds.
-- Whether a company is an exempt private company is s 4(1)'s question, and whether two companies are deemed related is s 6's: both are taken as facts
-- here (the seat asks them; sg-definitions.l4 and sg-groups.l4 compute them). Whether a person is "a director" is s 4(1) "director"'s: a fact too.
-- s 163A and s 163B are in sgb2-s163-loans-to-connected-persons.l4; the facts `an exception under section 163A or 163B applies` is theirs.

§ `Section 162(8): the family of a director`

DECLARE `s 162(8) relationship to the director` IS ONE OF
    `s 162(8) the director`
    `s 162(8) the director's spouse`
    `s 162(8) the director's son`
    `s 162(8) the director's adopted son`
    `s 162(8) the director's stepson`
    `s 162(8) the director's daughter`
    `s 162(8) the director's adopted daughter`
    `s 162(8) the director's stepdaughter`
    `s 162(8) another person`

-- src:13549 | (8) For the purpose of subsection (1), a reference to a director or
-- src:13550 | relevant director therein includes a reference to the director’s spouse,
-- src:13551 | son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter and
-- src:13552 | stepdaughter.
@ref s 162(8) (src:13549-13552)
GIVEN relationship IS A `s 162(8) relationship to the director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(8) the person counts as the director or relevant director` MEANS
    CONSIDER relationship
    WHEN `s 162(8) the director` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 162(8) the director's spouse` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 162(8) the director's son` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 162(8) the director's adopted son` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 162(8) the director's stepson` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 162(8) the director's daughter` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 162(8) the director's adopted daughter` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 162(8) the director's stepdaughter` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference to a director or relevant director therein includes a reference to the director's spouse, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter and stepdaughter" does not say that no other relative is included

§ `Section 162(11) and (12): the terms the section defines`

-- "conditional sale agreement" has the meaning given by section 2 of the Hire-Purchase Act 1969 (another Act: a supplied fact).
-- src:13570 | (11) In this section and section 163 —
-- src:13572 | “conditional sale agreement” has the meaning given by section 2
-- src:13573 | of the Hire‑Purchase Act 1969;
@ref s 162(11) "conditional sale agreement" (src:13570-13573)
GIVEN `the agreement is a conditional sale agreement as section 2 of the Hire-Purchase Act 1969 gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(11) "conditional sale agreement" the agreement is a conditional sale agreement` MEANS
    IF `the agreement is a conditional sale agreement as section 2 of the Hire-Purchase Act 1969 gives that meaning`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“conditional sale agreement” has the meaning given by section 2 of the Hire‑Purchase Act 1969" (a definition handed to another Act: the Act's own test is the fact asked)

-- src:13575 | “credit transaction” means a transaction under which one party
-- src:13576 | (called in this section and section 163 the creditor) —
-- src:13581 | (a) supplies any goods or disposes of any immovable
-- src:13582 | property under a hire‑purchase agreement or a
-- src:13583 | conditional sale agreement;
-- src:13585 | (b) leases or hires any immovable property or goods in
-- src:13586 | return for periodic payments; or
-- src:13588 | (c) otherwise disposes of immovable property or
-- src:13589 | supplies goods or services on the understanding
-- src:13590 | that payment (whether in a lump sum or instalments
-- src:13591 | or by way of periodic payments or otherwise) is to be
-- src:13592 | deferred;
@ref s 162(11) "credit transaction" (src:13575-13592)
GIVEN `the creditor supplies goods or disposes of immovable property under a hire-purchase agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor supplies goods or disposes of immovable property under a conditional sale agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor leases or hires immovable property or goods in return for periodic payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor otherwise disposes of immovable property or supplies goods or services on the understanding that payment is to be deferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(11) "credit transaction" the transaction is a credit transaction` MEANS
    IF    `the creditor supplies goods or disposes of immovable property under a hire-purchase agreement`
       OR `the creditor supplies goods or disposes of immovable property under a conditional sale agreement`
       OR `the creditor leases or hires immovable property or goods in return for periodic payments`
       OR `the creditor otherwise disposes of immovable property or supplies goods or services on the understanding that payment is to be deferred`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“credit transaction” means a transaction under which one party (called in this section and section 163 the creditor) — (a) supplies any goods or disposes of any immovable property under a hire‑purchase agreement or a conditional sale agreement; (b) leases or hires any immovable property or goods in return for periodic payments; or (c) otherwise disposes of immovable property or supplies goods or services on the understanding that payment ... is to be deferred"

-- src:13594 | “quasi‑loan” means a transaction under which one party (called
-- src:13595 | in this section and section 163 the creditor) agrees to pay, or
-- src:13596 | pays otherwise than pursuant to an agreement, a sum for
-- src:13597 | another (called in this section the borrower) or agrees to
-- src:13598 | reimburse, or reimburses otherwise than pursuant to an
-- src:13599 | agreement, expenditure incurred by another party for another
-- src:13600 | (called in this section and section 163 the borrower) —
-- src:13602 | (a) on terms that the borrower (or a person on the
-- src:13603 | borrower’s behalf) will reimburse the creditor; or
-- src:13605 | (b) in circumstances giving rise to a liability on the
-- src:13606 | borrower to reimburse the creditor;
@ref s 162(11) "quasi-loan" (src:13594-13606)
GIVEN `the creditor agrees to pay, or pays otherwise than pursuant to an agreement, a sum for the borrower` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor agrees to reimburse, or reimburses otherwise than pursuant to an agreement, expenditure incurred by another party for the borrower` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment or reimbursement is on terms that the borrower, or a person on the borrower's behalf, will reimburse the creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment or reimbursement is in circumstances giving rise to a liability on the borrower to reimburse the creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(11) "quasi-loan" the transaction is a quasi-loan` MEANS
    IF    (   `the creditor agrees to pay, or pays otherwise than pursuant to an agreement, a sum for the borrower`
           OR `the creditor agrees to reimburse, or reimburses otherwise than pursuant to an agreement, expenditure incurred by another party for the borrower`)
      AND (   `the payment or reimbursement is on terms that the borrower, or a person on the borrower's behalf, will reimburse the creditor`
           OR `the payment or reimbursement is in circumstances giving rise to a liability on the borrower to reimburse the creditor`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“quasi‑loan” means a transaction under which one party (called in this section and section 163 the creditor) agrees to pay, or pays otherwise than pursuant to an agreement, a sum for another ... or agrees to reimburse, or reimburses otherwise than pursuant to an agreement, expenditure incurred by another party for another ... (a) on terms that the borrower (or a person on the borrower’s behalf) will reimburse the creditor; or (b) in circumstances giving rise to a liability on the borrower to reimburse the creditor"

-- src:13608 | “services” means any thing other than goods or immovable
-- src:13609 | property.
@ref s 162(11) "services" (src:13608-13609)
GIVEN `the thing is goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is immovable property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(11) "services" the thing is services` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the thing is goods`) AND (NOT `the thing is immovable property`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“services” means any thing other than goods or immovable property"

-- src:13613 | (12) For the purposes of subsection (11) —
-- src:13615 | (a) a reference to the person to whom a quasi‑loan is made is a
-- src:13616 | reference to the borrower;
@ref s 162(12)(a) (src:13613-13616)
GIVEN `the person is the borrower under the quasi-loan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(12)(a) the person is the person to whom the quasi-loan is made` MEANS
    IF `the person is the borrower under the quasi-loan`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference to the person to whom a quasi‑loan is made is a reference to the borrower" (read as a definition that fixes who is meant: fork F-162-12 in NOTES.md)

-- src:13618 | (b) the liabilities of the borrower under a quasi‑loan include
-- src:13619 | the liabilities of any person who has agreed to reimburse
-- src:13620 | the creditor on behalf of the borrower;
@ref s 162(12)(b) (src:13618-13620)
GIVEN `the liability is the borrower's own liability under the quasi-loan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is that of a person who has agreed to reimburse the creditor on behalf of the borrower` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(12)(b) the liability is within the liabilities of the borrower under the quasi-loan` MEANS
    IF    `the liability is the borrower's own liability under the quasi-loan`
       OR `the liability is that of a person who has agreed to reimburse the creditor on behalf of the borrower`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the liabilities of the borrower under a quasi‑loan include the liabilities of any person who has agreed to reimburse the creditor on behalf of the borrower"

-- src:13622 | (c) a reference to the person for whose benefit a credit
-- src:13623 | transaction is entered into is a reference to the person to
-- src:13624 | whom goods, immovable property or services are supplied,
-- src:13629 | sold, leased, hired or otherwise disposed of under the
-- src:13630 | transaction; and
@ref s 162(12)(c) (src:13622-13630)
GIVEN `the person is the person to whom goods, immovable property or services are supplied, sold, leased, hired or otherwise disposed of under the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(12)(c) the person is the person for whose benefit the credit transaction is entered into` MEANS
    IF `the person is the person to whom goods, immovable property or services are supplied, sold, leased, hired or otherwise disposed of under the transaction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference to the person for whose benefit a credit transaction is entered into is a reference to the person to whom goods, immovable property or services are supplied, sold, leased, hired or otherwise disposed of under the transaction" (read as a definition that fixes who is meant: fork F-162-12)

-- src:13632 | (d) a reference to the supply of services means the supply of
-- src:13633 | anything other than goods or immovable property and
-- src:13634 | includes the transfer or disposal of choses in action or of
-- src:13635 | intellectual property rights.
@ref s 162(12)(d) (src:13632-13635)
GIVEN `the thing supplied is goods or immovable property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supply is a transfer or disposal of choses in action or of intellectual property rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(12)(d) the supply is a supply of services` MEANS
    IF `the supply is a transfer or disposal of choses in action or of intellectual property rights`
    THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text includes it in its own words: "includes the transfer or disposal of choses in action or of intellectual property rights"
    ELSE IF `the thing supplied is goods or immovable property`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference to the supply of services means the supply of anything other than goods or immovable property"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 162(1): the restricted transaction`

DECLARE `s 162(1) kind of dealing` IS ONE OF
    `s 162(1)(a) the company makes a loan or quasi-loan to a relevant director`
    `s 162(1)(b) the company enters into a guarantee or provides security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan made to a relevant director by another person`
    `s 162(1)(c) the company enters into a credit transaction as creditor for the benefit of a relevant director`
    `s 162(1)(d) the company enters into a guarantee or provides security in connection with a credit transaction entered into by any person for the benefit of a relevant director`
    `s 162(1)(e) the company takes part in an arrangement`
    `s 162(1)(f) the company arranges the assignment to it or assumption by it of rights, obligations or liabilities`
    `s 162(1) some other dealing`

-- A "relevant director": a director of the company, or of a company which by virtue of section 6 is deemed to be related to it (s 162(1)(a)(i), (ii)),
-- with s 162(8)'s family added.
-- src:13414 | (a) makes a loan or quasi‑loan to a director —
-- src:13416 | (i) of the company; or
-- src:13418 | (ii) of a company which by virtue of section 6 is deemed
-- src:13419 | to be related to that company,
-- src:13421 | (a) (called in this section a relevant director);
@ref s 162(1)(a) (src:13414-13421)
GIVEN relationship IS A `s 162(8) relationship to the director`
      `the director is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is a director of a company which by virtue of section 6 is deemed to be related to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(1)(a) the person is a relevant director` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the director is a director of the company`) AND (NOT `the director is a director of a company which by virtue of section 6 is deemed to be related to the company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a director — (i) of the company; or (ii) of a company which by virtue of section 6 is deemed to be related to that company, ... (called in this section a relevant director)" (a definition that names the two classes)
    ELSE `s 162(8) the person counts as the director or relevant director` relationship

-- The six kinds. The facts for kinds (e) and (f) are the other person's transaction, taken as facts: whether it "would have been a restricted
-- transaction under paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (f)" (for (e)), or "(a) to (e)" (for (f)), had the company entered into it.
-- src:13411 | 162.—(1) For the purposes of this section, a company makes a
-- src:13412 | restricted transaction if it —
-- src:13414 | (a) makes a loan or quasi‑loan to a director —
-- src:13416 | (i) of the company; or
-- src:13418 | (ii) of a company which by virtue of section 6 is deemed
-- src:13419 | to be related to that company,
-- src:13421 | (a) (called in this section a relevant director);
-- src:13423 | (b) enters into any guarantee or provides any security in
-- src:13424 | connection with a loan or quasi‑loan made to a relevant
-- src:13425 | director by any other person;
-- src:13430 | (c) enters into a credit transaction as creditor for the benefit of
-- src:13431 | a relevant director;
-- src:13433 | (d) enters into any guarantee or provides any security in
-- src:13434 | connection with a credit transaction entered into by any
-- src:13435 | person for the benefit of a relevant director;
-- src:13437 | (e) takes part in an arrangement under which —
-- src:13439 | (i) another person enters into a transaction that, if it had
-- src:13440 | been entered into by the company, would have been a
-- src:13441 | restricted transaction under paragraph (a), (b), (c),
-- src:13442 | (d) or (f); and
-- src:13444 | (ii) that person, pursuant to the arrangement, obtains a
-- src:13445 | benefit from the company or a company which by
-- src:13446 | virtue of section 6 is deemed to be related to that
-- src:13447 | company; or
-- src:13449 | (f) arranges the assignment to the company, or assumption by
-- src:13450 | the company, of any rights, obligations or liabilities under a
-- src:13451 | transaction that, if it had been entered into by the company,
-- src:13452 | would have been a restricted transaction under
-- src:13453 | paragraphs (a) to (e).
@ref s 162(1) (src:13411-13453)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 162(1) kind of dealing`
      `the person concerned is a relevant director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the other person's transaction would have been a restricted transaction under paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (f) if the company had entered into it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person, pursuant to the arrangement, obtains a benefit from the company or a company which by virtue of section 6 is deemed to be related to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction the company arranges the assignment or assumption of would have been a restricted transaction under paragraphs (a) to (e) if the company had entered into it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(1) the company makes a restricted transaction` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 162(1)(a) the company makes a loan or quasi-loan to a relevant director` THEN `the person concerned is a relevant director`
    WHEN `s 162(1)(b) the company enters into a guarantee or provides security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan made to a relevant director by another person` THEN `the person concerned is a relevant director`
    WHEN `s 162(1)(c) the company enters into a credit transaction as creditor for the benefit of a relevant director` THEN `the person concerned is a relevant director`
    WHEN `s 162(1)(d) the company enters into a guarantee or provides security in connection with a credit transaction entered into by any person for the benefit of a relevant director` THEN `the person concerned is a relevant director`
    WHEN `s 162(1)(e) the company takes part in an arrangement` THEN
        (IF    `the other person's transaction would have been a restricted transaction under paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (f) if the company had entered into it`
           AND `the other person, pursuant to the arrangement, obtains a benefit from the company or a company which by virtue of section 6 is deemed to be related to the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "takes part in an arrangement under which — (i) another person enters into a transaction that, if it had been entered into by the company, would have been a restricted transaction ...; and (ii) that person, pursuant to the arrangement, obtains a benefit from the company or a company which by virtue of section 6 is deemed to be related to that company" (a failed "if": a company makes a restricted transaction "if it" does one of the six things; marginal reading (a))
    WHEN `s 162(1)(f) the company arranges the assignment to it or assumption by it of rights, obligations or liabilities` THEN
        (IF `the transaction the company arranges the assignment or assumption of would have been a restricted transaction under paragraphs (a) to (e) if the company had entered into it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "arranges the assignment to the company, or assumption by the company, of any rights, obligations or liabilities under a transaction that, if it had been entered into by the company, would have been a restricted transaction under paragraphs (a) to (e)" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company makes a restricted transaction if it — (a) ... (f) ..." names six kinds of dealing, and a dealing of no kind is not a restricted transaction (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

-- (9) For (1)(e), the transaction is treated as entered into on the date of the arrangement.
-- src:13556 | (9) In determining for the purposes of this section whether a
-- src:13557 | transaction is a restricted transaction under subsection (1)(e), the
-- src:13558 | transaction is to be treated as having been entered into on the date of
-- src:13559 | the arrangement.
@ref s 162(9) (src:13556-13559)
GIVEN `the question is whether the transaction is a restricted transaction under subsection (1)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the arrangement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 162(9) the date on which the transaction is treated as entered into` MEANS
    IF `the question is whether the transaction is a restricted transaction under subsection (1)(e)`
    THEN JUST `the date of the arrangement`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In determining ... whether a transaction is a restricted transaction under subsection (1)(e), the transaction is to be treated as having been entered into on the date of the arrangement" says nothing for the other paragraphs of subsection (1)

§ `Section 162(10): what counts as prior approval`

-- "a reference to prior approval does not include any approval of the company that is given after the restricted transaction has been made,
-- provided for or entered into". An approval given on the same day is not "after" (fork F-162-10).
-- src:13563 | (10) For the purposes of this section, a reference to prior approval
-- src:13564 | does not include any approval of the company that is given after the
-- src:13565 | restricted transaction has been made, provided for or entered into (as
-- src:13566 | the case may be).
@ref s 162(10) (src:13563-13566)
GIVEN `the date the company gave its approval` IS A DATE
      `the date the restricted transaction was made, provided for or entered into` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(10) the approval counts as prior approval` MEANS
    IF `the date the company gave its approval` GREATER THAN `the date the restricted transaction was made, provided for or entered into`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference to prior approval does not include any approval of the company that is given after the restricted transaction has been made, provided for or entered into"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says which approvals are not prior; it does not say that an earlier approval is one, nor what the approval must contain

§ `Section 162(2): the company must not make a restricted transaction`

DECLARE `s 162(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 162(2) make a restricted transaction`

-- src:13457 | (2) Subject to subsections (3) and (4) and sections 163A and 163B,
-- src:13458 | a company (other than an exempt private company) must not make a
-- src:13459 | restricted transaction.
@ref s 162(2) (src:13457-13459)
GIVEN `the company is an exempt private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is within an exception in section 162(3) and (4) or in section 163A or 163B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(2) the section bars the company from making the restricted transaction` MEANS
    IF `the company is an exempt private company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a company (other than an exempt private company) must not make a restricted transaction" does not reach an exempt private company; "other than" is a scope limit with no "only" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c); fork F-162-2 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE IF `the transaction is within an exception in section 162(3) and (4) or in section 163A or 163B`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this section applies to any transaction which would otherwise be a restricted transaction that is" within section 162(3) (and "Sections 162 and 163 do not apply to anything done by a company" within section 163A; "Sections 162, 163 and 172 do not apply" within section 163B): flat negatives (fork F-162-2)
         ELSE JUST TRUE -- the text bars it in its own words (a flat negative, ruling N2): "a company (other than an exempt private company) must not make a restricted transaction"

-- The prohibition as a regulative rule (N2): the party is the company.
-- src:13457 | (2) Subject to subsections (3) and (4) and sections 163A and 163B,
-- src:13458 | a company (other than an exempt private company) must not make a
-- src:13459 | restricted transaction.
@ref s 162(2) (src:13457-13459)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the company is an exempt private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is within an exception in section 162(3) and (4) or in section 163A or 163B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 162(2) act`
`s 162(2) a company other than an exempt private company must not make a restricted transaction` MEANS
    IF `the company is an exempt private company` OR `the transaction is within an exception in section 162(3) and (4) or in section 163A or 163B`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY Company `the name of the company`
         SHANT `s 162(2) make a restricted transaction`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "a company that is not an exempt private company made a restricted transaction outside every exception"

§ `Section 162(3) and (4): the exceptions`

-- (3): "Subject to subsection (4), nothing in this section applies to any transaction which would otherwise be a restricted transaction that is" (a) to (d).
-- (a) and (b) are the two paragraphs (4) conditions. The paragraph (b) limit: "not more than one such restricted transaction may be outstanding at any time".
-- src:13463 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), nothing in this section applies to any
-- src:13464 | transaction which would otherwise be a restricted transaction that
-- src:13465 | is —
-- src:13467 | (a) made to or for the benefit of a relevant director to meet
-- src:13468 | expenditure incurred or to be incurred by him or her for the
-- src:13469 | purposes of the company or for the purpose of enabling
-- src:13470 | him or her to properly perform his or her duties as an
-- src:13471 | officer of the company;
-- src:13473 | (b) made to or for the benefit of a relevant director who is
-- src:13474 | engaged in the full‑time employment of the company or of
-- src:13475 | a corporation that is deemed to be related to the company,
-- src:13480 | as the case may be, for the purpose of purchasing or
-- src:13481 | otherwise acquiring a home occupied or to be occupied by
-- src:13482 | the director, except that not more than one such restricted
-- src:13483 | transaction may be outstanding at any time;
-- src:13485 | (c) made to or for the benefit of a relevant director who is
-- src:13486 | engaged in the full‑time employment of the company or of
-- src:13487 | a corporation that is deemed to be related to that company
-- src:13488 | (as the case may be) where the company has at a general
-- src:13489 | meeting approved of a scheme for the making of such
-- src:13490 | transaction to or for the benefit of employees of the
-- src:13491 | company and the restricted transaction is in accordance
-- src:13492 | with that scheme; or
-- src:13494 | (d) made to or for the benefit of a relevant director in the
-- src:13495 | ordinary course of business of a company whose ordinary
-- src:13496 | business includes the lending of money or the giving of
-- src:13497 | guarantees in connection with loans, quasi‑loans or credit
-- src:13498 | transactions made or entered into by other persons if the
-- src:13499 | activities of that company are regulated by any written law
-- src:13500 | relating to banking, finance companies or insurance or are
-- src:13501 | subject to supervision by the Monetary Authority of
-- src:13502 | Singapore.
@ref s 162(3) (src:13463-13502)
GIVEN `the transaction is made to or for the benefit of a relevant director to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by the director for the purposes of the company or for the purpose of enabling the director to properly perform the director's duties as an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is made to or for the benefit of a relevant director who is engaged in the full-time employment of the company or of a corporation that is deemed to be related to the company, for the purpose of purchasing or otherwise acquiring a home occupied or to be occupied by the director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another such restricted transaction for a home is outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is made to or for the benefit of a relevant director who is engaged in the full-time employment of the company or of a corporation that is deemed to be related to the company, under a scheme the company has approved at a general meeting, and is in accordance with that scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is made in the ordinary course of business of a company whose ordinary business includes the lending of money or the giving of guarantees in connection with loans, quasi-loans or credit transactions made or entered into by other persons, and its activities are regulated by a written law relating to banking, finance companies or insurance or are subject to supervision by the Monetary Authority of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions of subsection (4) are met for the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(3) the transaction is within an exception in subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF    (    `the transaction is made to or for the benefit of a relevant director to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by the director for the purposes of the company or for the purpose of enabling the director to properly perform the director's duties as an officer of the company`
           AND `the conditions of subsection (4) are met for the transaction`)
       OR (    `the transaction is made to or for the benefit of a relevant director who is engaged in the full-time employment of the company or of a corporation that is deemed to be related to the company, for the purpose of purchasing or otherwise acquiring a home occupied or to be occupied by the director`
           AND (NOT `another such restricted transaction for a home is outstanding`)
           AND `the conditions of subsection (4) are met for the transaction`)
       OR `the transaction is made to or for the benefit of a relevant director who is engaged in the full-time employment of the company or of a corporation that is deemed to be related to the company, under a scheme the company has approved at a general meeting, and is in accordance with that scheme`
       OR `the transaction is made in the ordinary course of business of a company whose ordinary business includes the lending of money or the giving of guarantees in connection with loans, quasi-loans or credit transactions made or entered into by other persons, and its activities are regulated by a written law relating to banking, finance companies or insurance or are subject to supervision by the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "nothing in this section applies to any transaction which would otherwise be a restricted transaction that is — (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; or (d) ..." lists four heads without "only"; a transaction in none of them is not said to be outside the section

-- (4): "Subsection (3)(a) or (b) does not authorise the making of any restricted transaction, except (a) with the prior approval of the company given at
-- a general meeting at which the purposes of the expenditure and the amount or extent of the restricted transaction are disclosed; or (b) on condition
-- that, if the prior approval of the company is not given as aforesaid at or before the next following annual general meeting, the amount of or liability
-- under the restricted transaction must be repaid or discharged (as the case may be) within 6 months from the conclusion of that meeting."
-- src:13506 | (4) Subsection (3)(a) or (b) does not authorise the making of any
-- src:13507 | restricted transaction, except —
-- src:13509 | (a) with the prior approval of the company given at a general
-- src:13510 | meeting at which the purposes of the expenditure and the
-- src:13511 | amount or extent of the restricted transaction are disclosed;
-- src:13512 | or
-- src:13514 | (b) on condition that, if the prior approval of the company is
-- src:13515 | not given as aforesaid at or before the next following
-- src:13516 | annual general meeting, the amount of or liability under the
-- src:13517 | restricted transaction must be repaid or discharged (as the
-- src:13518 | case may be) within 6 months from the conclusion of that
-- src:13519 | meeting.
@ref s 162(4) (src:13506-13519)
GIVEN `the transaction is within subsection (3)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company gave its prior approval at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purposes of the expenditure were disclosed at that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount or extent of the restricted transaction was disclosed at that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is made on condition that, if the prior approval of the company is not given at or before the next following annual general meeting, the amount or liability must be repaid or discharged within 6 months from the conclusion of that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(4) subsection (3)(a) or (b) authorises the making of the restricted transaction` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the transaction is within subsection (3)(a) or (b)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (3)(a) or (b) does not authorise the making of any restricted transaction, except ..." speaks of those two paragraphs only; a transaction within (3)(c) or (d) is outside it
    ELSE IF    (    `the company gave its prior approval at a general meeting`
                AND `the purposes of the expenditure were disclosed at that meeting`
                AND `the amount or extent of the restricted transaction was disclosed at that meeting`)
            OR `the transaction is made on condition that, if the prior approval of the company is not given at or before the next following annual general meeting, the amount or liability must be repaid or discharged within 6 months from the conclusion of that meeting`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (3)(a) or (b) does not authorise the making of any restricted transaction, except — (a) with the prior approval of the company given at a general meeting at which the purposes of the expenditure and the amount or extent of the restricted transaction are disclosed; or (b) on condition that ..." (a flat negative with an "except")

-- The 6 months of (4)(b): from the conclusion of the annual general meeting at which approval was not given.
-- src:13514 | (b) on condition that, if the prior approval of the company is
-- src:13515 | not given as aforesaid at or before the next following
-- src:13516 | annual general meeting, the amount of or liability under the
-- src:13517 | restricted transaction must be repaid or discharged (as the
-- src:13518 | case may be) within 6 months from the conclusion of that
-- src:13519 | meeting.
@ref s 162(4)(b) (src:13514-13519)
GIVEN `the date the next following annual general meeting concludes` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 162(4)(b) the last day on which the amount or liability must be repaid or discharged` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the next following annual general meeting concludes` 6 Months

-- src:13514 | (b) on condition that, if the prior approval of the company is
-- src:13515 | not given as aforesaid at or before the next following
-- src:13516 | annual general meeting, the amount of or liability under the
-- src:13517 | restricted transaction must be repaid or discharged (as the
-- src:13518 | case may be) within 6 months from the conclusion of that
-- src:13519 | meeting.
@ref s 162(4)(b) (src:13514-13519)
GIVEN `the date the next following annual general meeting concludes` IS A DATE
      `the date the amount was repaid or the liability discharged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 162(4)(b) the amount was repaid or the liability discharged within 6 months from the conclusion of the meeting` MEANS
    `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date the next following annual general meeting concludes` `the date the amount was repaid or the liability discharged` 6 Months

§ `Section 162(5): the directors who authorised the transaction`

-- src:13526 | (5) Where the prior approval of the company is not given as
-- src:13527 | required by the condition mentioned in subsection (4)(b), the
-- src:13528 | directors authorising the making of the restricted transaction are
-- src:13529 | jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company against any loss
-- src:13530 | arising therefrom.
@ref s 162(5) (src:13526-13530)
GIVEN `the transaction was made on the condition mentioned in subsection (4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prior approval of the company was given at or before the next following annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(5) the directors who authorised the transaction are jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company against any loss` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the transaction was made on the condition mentioned in subsection (4)(b)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "the condition mentioned in subsection (4)(b)", and a transaction not made on that condition is outside it
    ELSE IF `the prior approval of the company was given at or before the next following annual general meeting`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the prior approval of the company is not given as required by the condition mentioned in subsection (4)(b), the directors authorising the making of the restricted transaction are jointly and severally liable" (a failed "where": periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-162-5 in NOTES.md)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 162(6): the offence`

DECLARE `s 162(6) penalty` HAS
    `s 162(6) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 162(6) the longest imprisonment, in years` IS A NUMBER

-- src:13534 | (6) Where a company contravenes this section, any director who
-- src:13535 | authorises the making of the restricted transaction shall be guilty of an
-- src:13536 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:13537 | $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years.
@ref s 162(6) (src:13534-13537)
GIVEN `the company contravened section 162` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(6) the director is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company contravened section 162`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company contravenes this section, any director who authorises the making of the restricted transaction shall be guilty of an offence" (a failed "where": periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); split site (i), fork F-162-6 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE IF `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any director who authorises the making of the restricted transaction" describes the directors it reaches, with no "only" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c); split site (i))

-- src:13534 | (6) Where a company contravenes this section, any director who
-- src:13535 | authorises the making of the restricted transaction shall be guilty of an
-- src:13536 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:13537 | $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years.
@ref s 162(6) (src:13534-13537)
GIVEN `the company contravened section 162` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 162(6) penalty`
`s 162(6) the most the director may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the company contravened section 162` AND `the director authorised the making of the restricted transaction`
    THEN JUST (`s 162(6) penalty` OF 20000, 2)   -- "a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years" (the text says "or": whether both may be imposed it does not say)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is that of "any director who authorises the making of the restricted transaction" where "a company contravenes this section"

§ `Section 162(7): recovery of the amount`

-- src:13541 | (7) Nothing in this section operates to prevent the company from
-- src:13542 | recovering the amount of any loan, quasi‑loan, credit transaction or
-- src:13543 | arrangement or amount for which it becomes liable under any
-- src:13544 | guarantee entered into or in respect of any security given contrary to
-- src:13545 | this section.
@ref s 162(7) (src:13541-13545)
GIVEN `the amount is owed to the company under a loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction or arrangement made contrary to section 162, or is an amount for which the company becomes liable under a guarantee or security given contrary to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 162(7) section 162 operates to prevent the company from recovering the amount` MEANS
    IF `the amount is owed to the company under a loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction or arrangement made contrary to section 162, or is an amount for which the company becomes liable under a guarantee or security given contrary to it`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section operates to prevent the company from recovering the amount of any loan, quasi‑loan, credit transaction or arrangement or amount for which it becomes liable under any guarantee entered into or in respect of any security given contrary to this section" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of amounts under dealings made contrary to the section
